  "responseTimeMs": 12119,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe BIR assessment period when a taxpayer has filed a return is generally three years from the date of filing the return.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor taxpayers, this means they should maintain accurate records for at least three years following the filing of their tax returns, as they may be subject to audit and assessment during this period. After three years, the BIR generally cannot assess additional taxes unless specific exceptions apply, such as cases of fraud or failure to file a return.",
